tus="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HOSOKAWA HIROFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOTOURA MASAAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUGII HIKARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUNEKAWA TETSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOSOKAWA, HIROFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOTOURA, MASAAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGII, HIKARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUNEKAWA, TETSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A biaxially oriented polyester film suitable for use as a base film for media for high-density magnetic recording, which is reduced in track shifting and excellent in running durability and storage stability. The biaxially oriented polyester film has a width-direction dimensional change (A) of -0.3 to 0 % through 72-hour standing at 49  DEG C and 90 % RH under a machine-direction load of 32 MPa.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un film polyester à orientation biaxiale conçu pour être utilisé en tant que film de base d'un support d'enregistrement magnétique haute densité, qui présente un décalage des pistes réduit et qui s'avère posséder une excellente durabilité à l'utilisation et une excellente stabilité de stockage. Ce film polyester à orientation biaxiale présente une modification dimensionnelle (A) suivant sa largeur comprise entre  0,3 et 0 % en 72 heures de repos à 49  DEG C et 90 % de RH sous une charge de 32 Mpa dans le sens de la machine.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>